---
import SiteLayout from "../../components/SiteLayout.astro";
import { profile } from "../../data/profile";

const links = [
  { label: "GitHub", href: profile.github },
  { label: "LinkedIn", href: profile.linkedin },
  { label: "Email", href: profile.email ? "mailto:" + profile.email : "" },
].filter((item) => item.href);
---

<SiteLayout
  title="About | Beyond the Abstract"
  description="About the student behind Beyond the Abstract, the journal's editorial approach, and its developing research interests."
>
  <section class="page-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">About the author</span>
      <h1>A researcher in progress.</h1>
      <p>A Biotechnology undergraduate building the methods and habits needed to ask better computational questions.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="container profile-grid">
      <article class="profile-panel">
        <span class="eyebrow">Background</span>
        <h2>{profile.role}</h2>
        <p>{profile.introduction}</p>
        <p>My research experience includes faculty-supervised independent work and communicating progress and findings to faculty mentors. I describe that experience as supervised independent research and keep the scope of each contribution specific.</p>
        {links.length > 0 && (
          <div class="profile-links">
            {links.map((item) => <a href={item.href} target={item.href.startsWith("mailto:") ? undefined : "_blank"} rel={item.href.startsWith("mailto:") ? undefined : "noreferrer"}>{item.label} ↗</a>)}
          </div>
        )}
      </article>

      <article class="profile-panel">
        <span class="eyebrow">Developing research direction</span>
        <h2>Make evidence visible.</h2>
        <p>{profile.researchFocus}</p>
        <p>This direction raises practical questions: how to separate missing data from negative evidence, how to compare confidence measures, and how to express disagreement without hiding it behind a single score.</p>
        <div class="interest-list" aria-label="Current learning areas">
          <span>Computational biology</span><span>Protein function</span><span>Scientific ML</span>
          <span>Statistics</span><span>Mathematical modeling</span><span>Scientific software</span>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-tint">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><span class="eyebrow">How this journal works</span><h2>Three layers, kept distinct</h2></div>
        <p>Every research discussion should help readers see where the evidence ends and interpretation begins.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="topic-grid editorial-grid">
        <article class="topic-card"><span class="topic-index">01</span><h3>What the paper reports</h3><p>Methods, data, and findings are checked against the primary source and described with the right publication status.</p></article>
        <article class="topic-card"><span class="topic-index">02</span><h3>How I interpret it</h3><p>My explanation and criticism are labelled as interpretation, with assumptions and limitations kept in view.</p></article>
        <article class="topic-card"><span class="topic-index">03</span><h3>What remains open</h3><p>Potential applications and next questions are presented as possibilities to investigate, not established results.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Skills in development</span><h2>Building foundations, then applying them.</h2></div>
        <p>These are areas of active learning, not proficiency claims. The CV can later document concrete coursework, implementations, and research contributions.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="topic-grid editorial-grid">
        <article class="topic-card"><span class="topic-index">01</span><h3>Computing and data</h3><p>Python, programming fundamentals, data handling, and reproducible computational work.</p></article>
        <article class="topic-card"><span class="topic-index">02</span><h3>Biology and annotation</h3><p>Protein sequence and function, evidence sources, and careful interpretation of computational predictions.</p></article>
        <article class="topic-card"><span class="topic-index">03</span><h3>Mathematics and communication</h3><p>Statistics, probability, mathematical modeling, and clear explanations of research methods.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
